      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "$\\text{To convert a number from base ten to base eight, we divide it by 8 repeatedly until the quotient is 0. Then we read the remainders in reverse order to get the base eight representation. In this case, }473_{10} \\div 8 = 59 \\text{ remainder } 1.$$59 \\div 8 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 3.$$7 \\div 8 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 7$. Therefore, the base eight representation of }473_{10} \\text{ is } 731_{8}.$ The \\text{first digit from left to right is } \\boxed{7}.$. The answer is: 7",
