    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base \\(8\\) representation of \\(473_{10}\\), we need to determine the largest power of \\(8\\) that is less than or equal to \\(473\\). The powers of \\(8\\) are:\n\n\\[8^0 = 1\\]\n\\[8^1 = 8\\]\n\\[8^2 = 64\\]\n\\[8^3 = 512\\]\n\\[8^4 = 4096\\]\n\nSince \\(8^4 = 4096\\) is greater than \\(473\\), we use \\(8^3 = 512\\) as our largest power. Now, we divide \\(473\\) by \\(512\\) to find the coefficient of \\(8^3\\):\n\n\\[473 \\div 512 \\approx 0.924\\]\n\nThe integer part of the result is \\(0\\), so the coefficient of \\(8^3\\) is \\(0\\). This means that \\(473\\) is less than \\(512\\) but more than \\(512 - 512 = 0\\). To find the next power of \\(8\\) that is still less than \\(473\\), we use \\(8^2 = 64\\):\n\n\\[473 \\div 64 \\approx 7.365625\\]\n\nThe integer part of the result is \\(7\\), so the coefficient of \\(8^2\\) is \\(7\\). To find the next power of \\(8\\) that is less than \\(473\\), we use \\(8^1 = 8\\):\n\n\\[473 \\div 8 \\approx 59.125\\]\n\nThe integer part of the result is \\(59\\), so the coefficient of \\(8^1\\) is \\(59\\). Finally, to find the coefficient of \\(8^0\\), we subtract \\(473\\) from \\(512\\):\n\n\\[512 - 473 = 39\\]\n\nTherefore, the base \\(8\\) representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(5977_8\\), and the first digit from left to right is \\(5\\). The answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
